1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,753
The Ford Mustang GTD has no useful

2
00:00:02,753 --> 00:00:03,239
trunk.

3
00:00:03,419 --> 00:00:05,759
The space where your luggage would go

4
00:00:05,759 --> 00:00:07,466
is taken up by a cooler for

5
00:00:07,466 --> 00:00:08,225
the gearbox.

6
00:00:08,405 --> 00:00:10,977
And its rear wing can flatten itself

7
00:00:10,977 --> 00:00:12,977
out like a drag-racing flap,

8
00:00:12,977 --> 00:00:15,478
while two flaps under the nose open

9
00:00:15,478 --> 00:00:17,264
to keep the car balanced.

10
00:00:17,444 --> 00:00:20,377
These are two secrets hidden inside the

11
00:00:20,377 --> 00:00:21,656
Ford Mustang GTD,

12
00:00:21,656 --> 00:00:24,364
a Mustang that costs more than three

13
00:00:24,364 --> 00:00:26,244
hundred thousand dollars.

14
00:00:26,594 --> 00:00:27,771
One: the layout,

15
00:00:27,771 --> 00:00:29,757
with a gearbox at the back,

16
00:00:29,757 --> 00:00:32,994
a carbon-fibre driveshaft and a cooler where

17
00:00:32,994 --> 00:00:34,906
the cargo space should be.

18
00:00:35,086 --> 00:00:37,804
Two: the aerodynamics and ride height,

19
00:00:37,804 --> 00:00:40,379
which change shape when the car goes

20
00:00:40,379 --> 00:00:41,309
onto a track.

21
00:00:41,489 --> 00:00:43,493
Along the way we will look at

22
00:00:43,493 --> 00:00:44,392
the lap time,

23
00:00:44,392 --> 00:00:46,603
the price, and the racing car it

24
00:00:46,603 --> 00:00:47,294
came from.

25
00:00:47,474 --> 00:00:50,401
Every fact comes from a published source,

26
00:00:50,401 --> 00:00:52,258
listed in the description.

27
00:00:52,608 --> 00:00:54,400
Where sources disagree,

28
00:00:54,400 --> 00:00:55,336
we tell you.

29
00:00:55,516 --> 00:00:56,929
Where we do the maths,

30
00:00:56,929 --> 00:00:58,407
we label it as our own.

31
00:00:58,587 --> 00:01:01,261
And where a figure is a manufacturer's

32
00:01:01,261 --> 00:01:03,583
claim, rather than a measurement,

33
00:01:03,583 --> 00:01:04,287
we say so.

34
00:01:04,638 --> 00:01:05,996
Start with the car.

35
00:01:06,176 --> 00:01:08,875
Wikipedia says the current Mustang,

36
00:01:08,875 --> 00:01:10,108
the S six fifty,

37
00:01:10,108 --> 00:01:13,501
was unveiled on the fourteenth of September,

38
00:01:13,501 --> 00:01:17,664
twenty twenty-two, at the North American International

39
00:01:17,664 --> 00:01:20,671
Auto Show, and that production began on

40
00:01:20,671 --> 00:01:21,982
the first of May,

41
00:01:21,982 --> 00:01:25,298
twenty twenty-three, at Flat Rock Assembly.

42
00:01:25,478 --> 00:01:28,015
The GTD is the extreme version,

43
00:01:28,015 --> 00:01:31,125
unveiled on the seventeenth of August,

44
00:01:31,125 --> 00:01:35,300
twenty twenty-three, as a twenty twenty-five model.

45
00:01:35,650 --> 00:01:37,989
Its engine is a five point two

46
00:01:37,989 --> 00:01:40,796
litre supercharged Predator V eight,

47
00:01:40,796 --> 00:01:45,241
five thousand, one hundred sixty-three cubic centimetres,

48
00:01:45,241 --> 00:01:48,672
rated at eight hundred fifteen horsepower at

49
00:01:48,672 --> 00:01:51,324
seven thousand, four hundred r p m

50
00:01:51,324 --> 00:01:54,833
and six hundred sixty-four pound-feet at four

51
00:01:54,833 --> 00:01:56,704
thousand, eight hundred,

52
00:01:56,704 --> 00:01:58,498
according to Wikipedia.

53
00:01:58,678 --> 00:02:00,664
The page gives a top speed of

54
00:02:00,664 --> 00:02:02,788
two hundred two miles per hour.

55
00:02:02,968 --> 00:02:05,803
Those figures are consistent with what Kelley

56
00:02:05,803 --> 00:02:09,017
Blue Book reported in September twenty twenty-four.

57
00:02:09,367 --> 00:02:11,863
Not every source agrees on the power.

58
00:02:12,043 --> 00:02:14,528
Design News calls it an eight hundred

59
00:02:14,528 --> 00:02:17,551
horsepower beast, and the Torque Café article

60
00:02:17,551 --> 00:02:19,566
says reportedly eight hundred.

61
00:02:19,746 --> 00:02:21,042
By our arithmetic,

62
00:02:21,042 --> 00:02:24,354
the difference between eight hundred and eight

63
00:02:24,354 --> 00:02:27,018
hundred fifteen is under two percent,

64
00:02:27,018 --> 00:02:28,818
so the sources are close,

65
00:02:28,818 --> 00:02:30,114
not contradictory.

66
00:02:30,294 --> 00:02:32,324
We use eight hundred fifteen,

67
00:02:32,324 --> 00:02:34,984
which Ford's own figure appears to be.

68
00:02:35,334 --> 00:02:38,646
For scale, Wikipedia lists the ordinary Mustang

69
00:02:38,646 --> 00:02:41,466
GT at four hundred eighty horsepower and

70
00:02:41,466 --> 00:02:43,792
four hundred eighteen pound-feet,

71
00:02:43,792 --> 00:02:46,259
and the Dark Horse at five hundred.

72
00:02:46,439 --> 00:02:47,695
By our arithmetic,

73
00:02:47,695 --> 00:02:50,486
the GTD makes about seventy percent more

74
00:02:50,486 --> 00:02:53,208
power than the GT and about sixty-three

75
00:02:53,208 --> 00:02:55,511
percent more than the Dark Horse,

76
00:02:55,511 --> 00:02:58,651
and about fifty-nine percent more torque than

77
00:02:58,651 --> 00:02:59,140
either.

78
00:02:59,320 --> 00:03:01,027
It is not a tuned Mustang.

79
00:03:01,207 --> 00:03:03,066
It is a different car sharing a

80
00:03:03,066 --> 00:03:03,366
name.

81
00:03:03,716 --> 00:03:05,318
Here is the first secret.

82
00:03:05,498 --> 00:03:08,479
Wikipedia says the GTD has a rear-mounted

83
00:03:08,479 --> 00:03:11,678
transaxle, and Kelley Blue Book describes an

84
00:03:11,678 --> 00:03:15,022
eight-speed dual-clutch transaxle at the back,

85
00:03:15,022 --> 00:03:18,657
with a carbon-fibre driveshaft carrying power from

86
00:03:18,657 --> 00:03:20,475
the front-mounted engine.

87
00:03:20,655 --> 00:03:22,879
That is the same layout as some

88
00:03:22,879 --> 00:03:24,386
high-end sports cars:

89
00:03:24,386 --> 00:03:25,821
engine at the front,

90
00:03:25,821 --> 00:03:27,257
gearbox at the rear,

91
00:03:27,257 --> 00:03:28,979
to move weight rearward.

92
00:03:29,329 --> 00:03:32,003
The gearbox's maker is not named in

93
00:03:32,003 --> 00:03:33,531
the sources we read.

94
00:03:33,711 --> 00:03:38,078
Design News quotes Multimatic's chief technical officer,

95
00:03:38,078 --> 00:03:40,963
Holt, saying his team put a transaxle

96
00:03:40,963 --> 00:03:42,523
gearbox at the rear,

97
00:03:42,523 --> 00:03:44,706
without saying who built it.

98
00:03:44,886 --> 00:03:47,649
So we do not claim a manufacturer.

99
00:03:47,829 --> 00:03:49,334
A normal Mustang,

100
00:03:49,334 --> 00:03:53,229
by contrast, has the gearbox directly behind

101
00:03:53,229 --> 00:03:56,328
the engine, a six-speed manual or a

102
00:03:56,328 --> 00:03:59,869
ten-speed automatic, as Wikipedia lists.

103
00:04:00,219 --> 00:04:01,171
Now the trunk.

104
00:04:01,351 --> 00:04:03,750
Kelley Blue Book says the GTD has

105
00:04:03,750 --> 00:04:06,803
a pushrod rear suspension with hydraulics,

106
00:04:06,803 --> 00:04:09,711
and a transaxle cooler mounted where the

107
00:04:09,711 --> 00:04:11,892
cargo space would normally be.

108
00:04:12,072 --> 00:04:13,114
In other words,

109
00:04:13,114 --> 00:04:15,335
the part of the car that carries

110
00:04:15,335 --> 00:04:17,904
your bags now carries the cooling for

111
00:04:17,904 --> 00:04:18,737
the gearbox.

112
00:04:18,917 --> 00:04:21,378
A road-legal Mustang that has given up

113
00:04:21,378 --> 00:04:23,061
its boot to the racetrack.

114
00:04:23,412 --> 00:04:26,038
There is a small disagreement about the

115
00:04:26,038 --> 00:04:26,779
suspension.

116
00:04:26,959 --> 00:04:30,040
Kelley Blue Book and Motor One describe

117
00:04:30,040 --> 00:04:31,936
pushrod rear suspension,

118
00:04:31,936 --> 00:04:33,832
semi-active and inboard.

119
00:04:34,012 --> 00:04:37,936
Design News describes inboard suspension like many

120
00:04:37,936 --> 00:04:39,506
prototype race cars,

121
00:04:39,506 --> 00:04:42,489
with Multimatic's spool-valve dampers,

122
00:04:42,489 --> 00:04:45,157
and does not use the word pushrod.

123
00:04:45,337 --> 00:04:48,510
We think these descriptions are compatible,

124
00:04:48,510 --> 00:04:51,682
since pushrod systems are normally inboard,

125
00:04:51,682 --> 00:04:53,822
but the sources do not say so

126
00:04:53,822 --> 00:04:54,486
directly.

127
00:04:54,836 --> 00:04:56,821
Multimatic is the key name.

128
00:04:57,001 --> 00:04:59,618
Torque Café says it is a Canadian

129
00:04:59,618 --> 00:05:03,504
engineering and racing specialist that builds the

130
00:05:03,504 --> 00:05:05,170
Mustang GT3 race car,

131
00:05:05,170 --> 00:05:09,215
supplies the chassis for Porsche's nine sixty-three

132
00:05:09,215 --> 00:05:10,642
L M D h programme,

133
00:05:10,642 --> 00:05:13,180
and will assemble the GTD at its

134
00:05:13,180 --> 00:05:15,797
own facility rather than at Ford.

135
00:05:15,977 --> 00:05:18,833
Design News adds that it supplied the

136
00:05:18,833 --> 00:05:22,075
spool-valve shocks and notes it also built

137
00:05:22,075 --> 00:05:23,001
the Ford GT.

138
00:05:23,181 --> 00:05:26,235
The GTD is partly a Multimatic car.

139
00:05:26,585 --> 00:05:27,720
And every GTD,

140
00:05:27,720 --> 00:05:29,099
Design News says,

141
00:05:29,099 --> 00:05:32,018
has a lightweight carbon-fibre body.

142
00:05:32,198 --> 00:05:35,786
The Performance package adds magnesium wheels.

143
00:05:35,966 --> 00:05:38,348
The sources give no weight for the

144
00:05:38,348 --> 00:05:40,451
road car, so we cannot say how

145
00:05:40,451 --> 00:05:42,553
much lighter the GTD is than a

146
00:05:42,553 --> 00:05:43,675
regular Mustang.

147
00:05:43,855 --> 00:05:46,981
Wikipedia lists the standard Mustang GT at

148
00:05:46,981 --> 00:05:48,693
between three thousand,

149
00:05:48,693 --> 00:05:52,042
eight hundred twenty-seven and four thousand,

150
00:05:52,042 --> 00:05:53,084
twelve pounds.

151
00:05:53,264 --> 00:05:55,551
We leave the GTD's weight blank rather

152
00:05:55,551 --> 00:05:56,213
than guess.

153
00:05:56,564 --> 00:05:58,688
Why put the gearbox at the back?

154
00:05:58,868 --> 00:06:01,573
None of our sources say so directly.

155
00:06:01,753 --> 00:06:02,983
The usual reason,

156
00:06:02,983 --> 00:06:05,153
which is our reading and not a

157
00:06:05,153 --> 00:06:07,613
quotation, is weight distribution:

158
00:06:07,613 --> 00:06:10,796
moving a heavy component rearward balances a

159
00:06:10,796 --> 00:06:12,098
front-engined car.

160
00:06:12,278 --> 00:06:14,611
We cannot prove it was Ford's reasoning.

161
00:06:14,791 --> 00:06:17,102
What the sources do say is that

162
00:06:17,102 --> 00:06:19,860
the layout comes from the Mustang GT3

163
00:06:19,860 --> 00:06:22,767
racing programme, which we cover below.

164
00:06:23,118 --> 00:06:25,683
The second secret is aerodynamic.

165
00:06:25,863 --> 00:06:28,106
Design News says the GTD has a

166
00:06:28,106 --> 00:06:31,320
dual-element rear wing with an active flap.

167
00:06:31,500 --> 00:06:33,304
In high-downforce mode,

168
00:06:33,304 --> 00:06:36,520
it generates a large amount of downforce,

169
00:06:36,520 --> 00:06:38,559
but also substantial drag.

170
00:06:38,739 --> 00:06:41,992
A drag-reduction mode flattens the flap for

171
00:06:41,992 --> 00:06:43,278
higher top speed.

172
00:06:43,458 --> 00:06:45,963
Kelley Blue Book calls this a Drag

173
00:06:45,963 --> 00:06:49,426
Reduction System, which changes the wing angle.

174
00:06:49,776 --> 00:06:52,543
It also has a large front underwing

175
00:06:52,543 --> 00:06:55,231
with two flaps that open to reduce

176
00:06:55,231 --> 00:06:57,919
front downforce, Design News says,

177
00:06:57,919 --> 00:07:00,765
balancing the car when the rear wing

178
00:07:00,765 --> 00:07:01,397
changes.

179
00:07:01,577 --> 00:07:02,647
In plain terms,

180
00:07:02,647 --> 00:07:05,284
when the rear flattens out for speed,

181
00:07:05,284 --> 00:07:07,138
the front is relieved too,

182
00:07:07,138 --> 00:07:09,704
so the car does not become unstable.

183
00:07:09,884 --> 00:07:12,545
Neither source gives downforce figures,

184
00:07:12,545 --> 00:07:14,660
so we cannot say how much force

185
00:07:14,660 --> 00:07:15,956
each mode produces.

186
00:07:16,307 --> 00:07:18,037
The ride height changes too.

187
00:07:18,217 --> 00:07:21,189
Design News says the GTD has two

188
00:07:21,189 --> 00:07:24,439
ride heights and two sets of spring

189
00:07:24,439 --> 00:07:24,997
rates.

190
00:07:25,177 --> 00:07:26,293
In track mode,

191
00:07:26,293 --> 00:07:29,484
the front drops by forty millimetres and

192
00:07:29,484 --> 00:07:31,000
the rear by thirty,

193
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:31,957
adding rake.

194
00:07:32,137 --> 00:07:34,111
The rear spring rate doubles,

195
00:07:34,111 --> 00:07:36,289
and the front rises by two point

196
00:07:36,289 --> 00:07:37,106
eight times.

197
00:07:37,286 --> 00:07:38,490
By our arithmetic,

198
00:07:38,490 --> 00:07:41,231
the front drops ten millimetres more than

199
00:07:41,231 --> 00:07:43,639
the rear, which tilts the car's nose

200
00:07:43,639 --> 00:07:44,240
downward.

201
00:07:44,591 --> 00:07:46,286
Hold on to what that means.

202
00:07:46,466 --> 00:07:47,447
The same car,

203
00:07:47,447 --> 00:07:49,033
parked in a driveway,

204
00:07:49,033 --> 00:07:50,694
rides like a road car,

205
00:07:50,694 --> 00:07:53,035
and on a circuit it changes its

206
00:07:53,035 --> 00:07:55,754
stance, its stiffness and its wings.

207
00:07:55,934 --> 00:07:58,430
Few road cars do all three.

208
00:07:58,610 --> 00:08:01,048
The sources do not give ride height

209
00:08:01,048 --> 00:08:02,650
numbers in normal mode,

210
00:08:02,650 --> 00:08:04,740
so we cannot tell you how high

211
00:08:04,740 --> 00:08:05,645
the car sits.

212
00:08:05,825 --> 00:08:08,001
Only the change is documented:

213
00:08:08,001 --> 00:08:10,249
forty millimetres at the front.

214
00:08:10,599 --> 00:08:13,933
The sources also suggest the aerodynamics were

215
00:08:13,933 --> 00:08:15,962
part of a deliberate target.

216
00:08:16,142 --> 00:08:19,194
Design News quotes chief engineer Greg Goodall

217
00:08:19,194 --> 00:08:21,051
saying that all of it was in

218
00:08:21,051 --> 00:08:23,638
the quest for a sub-seven-minute lap of

219
00:08:23,638 --> 00:08:26,888
the Nürburgring, and that the Performance package

220
00:08:26,888 --> 00:08:28,414
is meant to deliver it.

221
00:08:28,594 --> 00:08:30,289
That target became public.

222
00:08:30,469 --> 00:08:32,064
Ford's chief executive,

223
00:08:32,064 --> 00:08:34,838
Jim Farley, promised at the car's August

224
00:08:34,838 --> 00:08:37,958
twenty twenty-three debut that it would break

225
00:08:37,958 --> 00:08:40,593
seven minutes, according to AutoGuide.

226
00:08:40,943 --> 00:08:42,266
The promise was kept.

227
00:08:42,446 --> 00:08:45,350
AutoGuide reports that the GTD set a

228
00:08:45,350 --> 00:08:47,690
certified lap of six minutes,

229
00:08:47,690 --> 00:08:51,079
fifty-seven point six eight seconds on the

230
00:08:51,079 --> 00:08:53,983
twelve point nine mile Nordschleife,

231
00:08:53,983 --> 00:08:56,000
on the seventh of August,

232
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:59,550
twenty twenty-four, driven by Dirk Müller of

233
00:08:59,550 --> 00:09:01,405
Multimatic Motorsports.

234
00:09:01,585 --> 00:09:05,793
Wikipedia gives six fifty-seven point six eight

235
00:09:05,793 --> 00:09:06,241
five.

236
00:09:06,421 --> 00:09:09,191
Ford said the car was otherwise stock,

237
00:09:09,191 --> 00:09:10,431
with a roll cage,

238
00:09:10,431 --> 00:09:14,003
competition seat and five-point harness added for

239
00:09:14,003 --> 00:09:15,024
certification.

240
00:09:15,374 --> 00:09:18,161
AutoGuide says Ford claimed it was the

241
00:09:18,161 --> 00:09:22,269
fastest American production car around the Nordschleife,

242
00:09:22,269 --> 00:09:26,010
the fifth-fastest production sports car on official

243
00:09:26,010 --> 00:09:29,677
records, and the second-fastest front-engined one.

244
00:09:29,857 --> 00:09:32,156
The previous American record,

245
00:09:32,156 --> 00:09:34,851
it says, was the Dodge Viper ACR's

246
00:09:34,851 --> 00:09:37,229
seven oh one point oh three in

247
00:09:37,229 --> 00:09:38,576
twenty seventeen.

248
00:09:38,756 --> 00:09:40,080
By our arithmetic,

249
00:09:40,080 --> 00:09:42,653
the GTD was about three point three

250
00:09:42,653 --> 00:09:45,447
seconds, or eight tenths of a percent,

251
00:09:45,447 --> 00:09:46,036
quicker.

252
00:09:46,386 --> 00:09:49,744
The fastest front-engined car at that time

253
00:09:49,744 --> 00:09:52,702
was the Mercedes-AMG G T Black Series

254
00:09:52,702 --> 00:09:54,221
from twenty twenty,

255
00:09:54,221 --> 00:09:56,860
at six forty-eight point oh four,

256
00:09:56,860 --> 00:09:58,459
nine seconds faster,

257
00:09:58,459 --> 00:09:59,818
the article says.

258
00:09:59,998 --> 00:10:03,505
Other faster production cars it lists include

259
00:10:03,505 --> 00:10:06,155
two Porsche nine eleven G T threes

260
00:10:06,155 --> 00:10:07,558
with Manthey kits,

261
00:10:07,558 --> 00:10:09,506
a nine eleven G T three R

262
00:10:09,506 --> 00:10:11,377
S, and a nine nine one G

263
00:10:11,377 --> 00:10:13,247
T two R S with a Manthey

264
00:10:13,247 --> 00:10:13,559
kit.

265
00:10:13,739 --> 00:10:15,755
Porsche is the benchmark,

266
00:10:15,755 --> 00:10:18,336
even in a story about a Mustang.

267
00:10:18,687 --> 00:10:20,382
The record did not last.

268
00:10:20,562 --> 00:10:24,053
Wikipedia says the GTD ran six fifty-two

269
00:10:24,053 --> 00:10:26,847
point oh seven two in May twenty

270
00:10:26,847 --> 00:10:30,513
twenty-five, and that the Corvette ZR1 and

271
00:10:30,513 --> 00:10:33,481
ZR1X, at six fifty point seven six

272
00:10:33,481 --> 00:10:36,973
three and six forty-nine point two seven

273
00:10:36,973 --> 00:10:39,068
five, beat it that July.

274
00:10:39,248 --> 00:10:42,091
Then, on the seventeenth of April,

275
00:10:42,091 --> 00:10:46,941
twenty twenty-six, a pre-production GTD Competition lapped

276
00:10:46,941 --> 00:10:49,951
in six forty point eight three five,

277
00:10:49,951 --> 00:10:51,790
with magnesium wheels,

